  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is greater than $10$ and prime. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{is greater than}\\,10}_{⏟}}_{F}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $F∧G.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is negative. This corresponds to $H.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{ is greater than}\\,10\\,\\text{and prime}}_{⏟}}_{F∧G}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{H},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(F∧G)∨H.$",
